description: 'Store crash-consistency tests (review P1-14). Current state: GOOD baseline
  already exists — tests/wal_crash.rs has 3 tests (wal_basic_durability_and_replay,
  wal_group_commit_durability, wal_survives_kill_9) and tests/wal_property.rs (225
  LOC) runs proptest with randomized op sequences (insert/update/delete/destroy) and
  randomized crash points. Remaining gap per review: torn-write simulation (truncate
  WAL at random byte offsets mid-record, not just op boundaries), multi-store crash
  interleavings, and recovery idempotence (recover twice == recover once). Definition
  of done: extend tests/wal_property.rs with torn-tail truncation strategy + double-recovery
  invariant; keep total CI runtime bounded (~5 min cap per review B.9).'
